{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":75541092,"ns":0,"title":"Epicurean paradox","extract":"The Epicurean paradox is a logical dilemma about the problem of evil attributed to the Greek philosopher Epicurus, who argued against the existence of a god who is simultaneously omniscient, omnipotent, and omnibenevolent.","description":"Logical dilemma in philosophy","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}